sdl3-mixer-mpg123
=================

This crate is a modified version of libmpg123: a translation into Rust of
the copy of libmpg123 1.33.7 ("MPEG Audio Decoder library", Copyright (c)
1995-2020 by Michael Hipp and others, "the mpg123 project"; see AUTHORS)
that SDL_mixer 3.3.0 vendors (external/mpg123/ at SDL_mixer revision
df66ae893c91b0f6fa5d026a195bb278213d007d, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer).

It is NOT the original libmpg123, nor SDL_mixer's copy of it.

How and when it was changed: on 2026-10-17, the parts of that copy that
SDL_mixer's build of it (its CMake port, as SDL_mixer's CMakeLists.txt
configures it) reaches from SDL_mixer's MPG123 decoder were translated,
function by function, into the Rust source files in src/, which keep the
original copyright notices and comments; each file says so in a line under
its copyright notice. Those are, from src/libmpg123/: libmpg123.c,
gapless.h, frame.h, frame.c, mpg123lib_intern.h, parse.h, parse.c,
mpeghead.h, reader.h, readers.c (its stream readers, without the feeder
and buffered ones), id3.h, id3.c, icy.h, icy.c, stringbuf.c, index.h,
index.c, format.c, optimize.h, optimize.c (the generic decoder only),
synths.h, layer1.c, layer2.c, layer3.c, dct64.c, synth.h, synth_mono.h,
sample.h, synth.c, synth_8bit.c, synth_real.c, synth_s32.c (their 1:1
synths), equalizer.c (as the decoders use it), tabinit.c, getbits.h,
newhuffman.h, the precomputed tables (costabs.h, l12tabs.h, l3tabs.h,
l2tables.h, l3bandgain.h) and the constants of the public headers
(mpg123.h, fmt123.h). Not translated: the assembly decoders, the
dithered generic one, the downsampling and NtoM resampling synths, the
feeder reader, the equalizer API functions, lfs_wrap.c, icy2utf8.c
(whose BSD-style terms differ), and the programs, libout123 and
libsyn123, which SDL_mixer doesn't build. The translation works on Rust types (slices,
vectors and enums rather than pointers, unions and function pointers) and
does something defined where corrupt input or unusual flags make the C
code read out of bounds (the places marked "FIXME (upstream)" in the
source). Otherwise it decodes bit-for-bit what the C code does, which its
tests check. The changes are freely available as part of
https://github.com/danielpclark/SDL.

License
-------

libmpg123 is licensed under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 2.1: see COPYING (verbatim from SDL_mixer's copy of
mpg123, with the license texts; it also carries the GPL, version 2, which
the LGPL lets a recipient switch to, but which no file of the library is
under). So is this crate: its SPDX license expression is "LGPL-2.1-only"
(COPYING doesn't offer a later version).

Unlike the rest of the repository, which is under the zlib license, this
crate is under the LGPL. sdl3-mixer uses it to decode MP3 (and MPEG audio
layers I and II) through its `mpg123` Cargo feature, which is on by
default; build sdl3-mixer with `default-features = false` to leave it
out, and MP3 then goes to the zlib-licensed dr_mp3 decoder (as it does
in an SDL_mixer built without libmpg123).

The test data in testdata/ (small MPEG audio files made from a synthetic
signal) is generated by tools/gen_mpg123_testdata.py in the repository.
